tries it's majority female. Computer programming was once majority female; then it flipped. Something deeper than pure nature is at work. So my caution isn't about avoiding an uncomfortable truth. It's about refusing to take a statistical pattern and turn it into a prescriptive law about what it means to be a man or a woman. That's a leap I won't make, not because I'm inconsistent, but because I think it's intellectually dishonest to treat those two kinds of claims as the same. That's my honest answer. I don't expect it to change your mind. But I hope it clarifies why my earlier answers weren't just selective cowardice.
